+======================================================================+
|           TERRAFORM LIFECYCLE: create_before_destroy                 |
+======================================================================+

WHAT IT DOES
------------
create_before_destroy = true

-> Creates the NEW resource first
-> Then destroys the OLD resource
-> Prevents downtime during replacement


DEFAULT BEHAVIOR (WITHOUT LIFECYCLE)
------------------------------------

Example:

resource "aws_instance" "app_server" {
  ami           = "ami-xxxx"
  instance_type = "t3.medium"
}

When instance_type changes:
1) Destroy old instance
2) Create new instance

Result: DOWNTIME


WITH create_before_destroy
--------------------------

Example:

resource "aws_instance" "app_server" {
  ami           = "ami-xxxx"
  instance_type = "t3.large"

  lifecycle {
    create_before_destroy = true
  }
}

What happens:
1) Terraform creates the NEW instance first
2) Waits until it is fully provisioned
3) Then destroys the OLD instance

Result: ZERO or MINIMAL downtime


REAL-WORLD ANALOGY
------------------
BAD:
- Cancel apartment lease
- Then look for new apartment

GOOD:
- Rent new apartment
- Move furniture
- Then cancel old lease


WHEN TO USE
-----------
- Production EC2 instances
- Databases
- Load-balanced services
- Customer-facing applications


DEVOPS CONCEPT
--------------
Enables blue-green style replacement
instead of destructive replacement.
